Aerie-Purpose: Replace Helium's layout picker and Zen toggles on the Appearance page with an empty "Sidebar" section, and add that section's title string.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page (appearance_layout_page.ts, appearance_layout_page.html.ts), chrome/app (generated_resources.grd and its gritdeps), chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_localized_strings_provider.cc)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #177. Helium's layout page chooses between four layouts and turns Zen mode on; Aerie has one
layout, the sidebar, so nothing there can be chosen (patches/sidebar/0021 also stops Settings from
writing those prefs). The page keeps its element name, view id and place, so the Appearance page
index and the router are untouched, and shows a section called "Sidebar" with nothing in it. The
slices that add sidebar settings (side, density, auto-hide, themes) fill it. This also takes away
the right-align, expand-on-hover, centred and minimal location bar and progress bar toggles that
were on that page: the first two belong to the Helium strip that the sidebar replaces, the next two
to the toolbar that moves into the sidebar, and the progress bar toggle goes with the page's other
rows. A sidebar setting can bring any of them back.
The title string is in the overlay's aerie_sidebar_strings.grdp.

